// Lyra OS - Odisseia (v1)
//
// polkit's stock /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/50-default.rules starts
// polkit._suse_admin_groups as an empty array; empty means its
// addAdminRule falls back to ["unix-user:0"] - i.e. every auth_admin
// pkexec/polkit action prompts for root's password specifically. root is
// locked ("!" in kiwi/config.xml) on both the live session and the
// installed system (installer/src/service/operations/deploy.rs disables
// it), so that prompt is impossible to satisfy - the polkit analog of the
// sudo "Defaults targetpw" issue fixed for sudoers/10-installer.
//
// liveuser and the sudo user the installer creates are both in "wheel"
// (kiwi/config.xml, deploy.rs REQUIRED_USER_GROUPS), so adding wheel here
// lets them authenticate admin actions with their own password instead.
//
// Filename must sort after "50-default.rules" - rule files from /etc and
// /usr/share are merged into one alphabetically ordered list, and this
// only takes effect if it runs after that file's `= []` reset.
polkit._suse_admin_groups.push("wheel");
